From b4bddcf28b91e453af16f64b1755877c11003e9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamar Shuster <tshuster@syr.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:03:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] TM09-131 fix(web): a vertical touch drag no longer passes the
 card

Swipeable listing cards: cover the touch half of the acceptance criteria
and fix the bug that turned up while doing it.

- SwipeCard: handle pointercancel on its own and snap the card back. With
  touch-action: pan-y the browser cancels the pointer as soon as a touch
  goes vertical, and Chrome reports that cancel at clientX 0. It was routed
  through onPointerUp, which read it as a long left drag, so trying to
  scroll on a card silently passed it.
- e2e: add touchDrag(), which drives Chrome's real touch pipeline over CDP
  (page.mouse only makes mouse pointers), and swipe-touch.spec.ts: touch
  right saves, touch left passes, the page does not scroll mid-swipe, and a
  vertical drag neither swipes nor opens the card. Runs in the mobile
  project only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
